# Build context for apps/worker/Dockerfile.selfhost ONLY. BuildKit prefers
# `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the root `/.dockerignore`, and the root file is the
# MANAGED recipe's context — pnpm manifests, pinned by a workspace test to the organizer's
# compile closure. This is the same closure in the published tree's npm shape.
#
# Same discipline: DENY EVERYTHING, RE-ADMIT THE BUILD'S INPUTS. An import reaching outside
# the packages below resolves to a workspace link whose target holds only a manifest, and
# the bundle FAILS to build — the organizer's dependency boundary, enforced by the context.
*

# Workspace manifests and the pinned resolution — `npm ci` validates the lockfile against
# every workspace manifest it finds.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!apps/*/package.json
!packages/*/package.json

# The build steps the image runs: the host bundler and the esbuild loader it shares with the
# engine build (the version pin lives there).
!scripts/bundle-host.mjs
!scripts/engine-bundle.mjs

# The organizer's compile closure — core and db because the organizer names them, db-mail
# because db does. The workspace test that pins the managed context's package lines is the
# same authority for these.
!apps/worker
!packages/core
!packages/db
!packages/db-mail

# …minus anything inside them that must never be copied in: no test trees, no stale local
# compile output, no previous bundle run.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/test
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/.claude

# Secrets never enter an image layer; every value arrives as a compose/service variable.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
